WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.841
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.841 --> 00:00:05.188
which takes about forty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:08.287
You'll explain the two writer
patterns Gate 2 allows,

4
00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:10.738
and why it allows only
one of them at a time.

5
00:00:10.738 --> 00:00:15.376
You'll explain why Gate 2 names one
approver system for each authority class.

6
00:00:15.376 --> 00:00:19.237
You'll run the writer check
over two configuration exports,

7
00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:22.862
and interpret each Finding,
Warn and Info line it prints.

8
00:00:22.862 --> 00:00:26.404
And you'll verify that the alias
list and the directory name

9
00:00:26.404 --> 00:00:29.801
are inputs a reviewer checks,
not things the tool guesses.

10
00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.637
You need Module 2 first.

11
00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:37.424
For the Graph export in Lab 2, the Microsoft
Automation path's first module helps.

12
00:00:37.424 --> 00:00:40.580
Lab 1 runs on fixtures, with no tenant.
